wlanpi-grafana (1.1.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * First working release on Debian trixie with Grafana 13.
  * Fix installation with Grafana 13. The postinst called the deprecated
    `grafana-cli`, which in Grafana 13 runs the grafana binary without
    --homepath/--config and fails with "Grafana-server Init Failed",
    aborting the postinst (set -e) and dpkg configure. Use the supported
    `grafana cli` wrapper, which supplies the package paths.
  * Pin Grafana to the 13.x series. Grafana 13 introduced the `grafana cli`
    wrapper and removed the old `grafana-cli`/`grafana-server` binaries.
  * Talk to Grafana directly on port 3000 in check-token.sh and to-grafana.sh.
    The wlanpi-webui nginx /app/grafana location requires a webui session
    (auth_request), so local API calls with basic auth were redirected to the
    login page and service account/token creation failed.
  * Look up the wlanpi service account ID and recreate its token cleanly
    instead of assuming the account ID is 2 and the token name is unused.
  * Ensure the self-signed-grafana TLS key is group-readable by grafana. When
    wlanpi-core generated it before the grafana group existed, Grafana could
    not read the key and crash-looped on startup.
  * chown /var/lib/grafana/plugins to grafana after installing plugins as
    root, otherwise Grafana cannot install or update plugins at runtime.
  * Make build-time plugin installs non-fatal and add plugins.preinstall as a
    runtime fallback, so a plugin catalog outage cannot fail the image build
    or leave the image without the spectrum panels.
  * The Grafana apt repository must be configured before this package is
    installed; the `grafana` dependency is not provided by Debian or the
    WLAN Pi repositories.

 -- Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>  Mon, 21 Sep 2026 18:00:00 -0400

wlanpi-grafana (1.0.11-3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Drop python3-distutils from Build-Depends and Pre-Depends. It was removed
    in Debian trixie (distutils is gone from Python 3.12+); python3-setuptools
    (already a build dep) and the venv-bundled setuptools provide it. This
    unblocks the trixie build/install.
  * Build for Debian trixie only.

 -- Josh Schmelzle <josh@joshschmelzle.com>  Wed, 15 Jul 2026 03:32:40 -0400

